please write this like this:

```c
if (xen_dom0 < 0)
        return xen_dom0;
if (xen_dom0 == 0)
        goto finish;

r = VIRTUALIZATION_NONE;
…
```

i.e. nest the jumps (i.e. the return + goto) in the conditional blocks, and thus get rid of needless indentation of the main codepath here. i.e. less indentation is a good thing

it only makes sense to do this test if `r == VIRTUALIZATION_XEN` already applies, no? i.e. shouldn't the block be:

```c
…
else if (r == VIRTUALIZATION_XEN) {
        /* … */
        xen_dom0 = detect_vm_xen_dom0();
        if (xen_dom0 < 0)
                return xen_dom0;
        if (xen_dom0 > 0) {
                /* If we are in Xen Dom0, then we don't consider this a VM environment, because it is the domain that manages the hardware, i.e. it's the host, not the payload.
                   Don't bother with the other checks either in that case then, since we are only interested in the "innermost" VM environment, and if that's Xen Dom0, then we are not virtualized. */ 
                r = VIRTUALIZATION_NONE; 
                goto finish;
        }

        /* Otherwise: we detected Xen, and are not Dom0, hence return this as Xen */
        goto finish;
} else if (r != VIRTUALIZATION_NONE)
        goto finish;
…
```
